    <DataNode elementId="ASN" textLabel="L-asparagine" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="DCXYFEDJOCDNAF-REOHCLBHSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="1475.005126953125" centerY="50.0" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco">|FRAME: ASN &quot;Asparagine&quot;| (Asn) is one of the proteinogenic amino acids. It was the first proteinogenic amino acid to be isolated, back in 1806, from asparagus juice, hence its name. The accurate structure of the molecule was reported only in 1888 |CITS: [Piutti88]|. Piutti also discovered the existence of |FRAME: CPD-3633| two years earlier |CITS: [Piutti86]|.</Comment>
